//  || 26443 THE ABRUPT-MOTION STENCIL FLICKER IS FINALIZED (full ledger at the trajectory bound, directly under KH_TRN_FLOOR_RESIDUAL; 223 reverts the whole fold - census-verified free). FIELD (dump1 on 26442, 3588 flushes, 512-row trace; operator: the flicker "used to be fixed but is now more prevalent - finalize once and for all"): seamTrnEvent 1 on 8 of 512 after 26406 recorded zero, ALL floor-branch (bnd 0.3000, resumed step 0.51-0.55 refused, primeCamDxM[k+1] == camStepM - the one-frame parallax, complete coverage). TWO SUB-CLASSES: (a) STALL-MANUFACTURED (5/8) - the publication stream repeats the camera one row in every 11-12 during steady 0.52 m motion (sim/render beat; camStepM, compCamStepM and the seam fetch stall together one seam-phase row apart), two zero rows put both refs at 0.0000 mid-motion and the resume meets a "stationary" floor; (b) INSTANT-VELOCITY DEAD-STOP STARTS (3/8 + 26433's two) - Zeus/spectator 0 -> 0.51 in one frame, no partial first step for the 26405 ratio line, and magnitude cannot separate 0.51-1.24 legit from 2.593 foreign (rule 1.2). THE FOLD, both default: (i) RECENT-VELOCITY RING - the floor classification references the max of the last four APPLIED latch steps, so manufactured zeros cannot reclassify a moving camera (a true stop drains it in ~4 runs / 80 ms and the floor stands); (ii) WITNESS GATE on floor refusals only - the fetch is taken when its own projection near agrees with the identity-keyed census near AND the census near agrees with the SNIFF near, both on the chain's existing 10 percent bar (26312), no new constant. The sniff leg is what the 26433 sketch lacked: 26326's poisoned-witness class (census AND fetch both foreign, ~2 percent of flicker rows) defeats census-vs-fetch alone, and the sniff - the engine's own upload for OUR window, ratio 1.000000 on 511/511 - cannot be foreign. Near-ramp starts abstain (census k+1 vs sniff k) and fall back to today's refusal: the fail direction is the status quo. The hoist is a