// available - 7817 head / 9751 tail - rather than the nearest one, so the next
// addition on either side has room instead of landing straight back on the cap.
// Adjacent literals concatenate, so the shader source is byte-identical.
// ==========================================================================
// 26262 THE ENGINE'S OWN VIEW ROTATION, COPIED GPU-SIDE AT THE INJECTION.
//
// WHY IT IS HERE AND NOT IN CBFrame. The value must be SAME-FRAME. Our harvest
// of the engine's view (g_ls.frame_view, out of the cascade-upload stream) is
// written 589 times a frame and alternates between this frame's camera and the
// next - measured, not supposed: injAdoptRotMax 0.0198 deg says the injection
// adopts it faithfully, and svReprojPxMean 95 px says what it adopted was wrong.
// A CPU readback of the engine's constant buffer is a frame late, which is fatal
// for a value and harmless for an address - so the ADDRESS is located once
// through a staging Map and the VALUE is CopySubresourceRegion'd every frame,
// GPU to GPU, no stall.
//
// THE LAYOUT, DECODED FROM THREE CAPTURES AND VERIFIED ARITHMETICALLY. The
// engine keeps ONE view constant buffer, bound at b2 by the volume-pass shader
// family and b3 by the colour-pass family - same resource, same bytes:
//     byte   0..47   identity 3x3 with the CAMERA in the translation column
//     byte  64..111  THE VIEW ROTATION, rows = camera axes, row 3 = (0,0,0,1)
//     byte 224       the camera position again, float3 + 1
// and the projection sits at b1 byte 0. With E the rotation block and P the
// projection, transpose(E) x P reproduces our composite's own view_proj to
// 1.6e-06 on every element, m11 folding included (0.975983 * 1.777778 =
// 1.735081, captured as 1.735081). So the transform is
//     clip = (worldPos - camera) x transpose(E) x P
