// ===========================================================================
// 26195 ENGINE DISTANCE HAZE (PSC_HazePars, sky CB row 14).
//
// THE FAULT THIS CLOSES: world geometry carries a blue distance wash our
// meshes never received - visible as a crisp red box against hazed hills.
// It is NOT the fog: the engine runs this as a SECOND extinction integral
// multiplied into the same transmittance, and it is armed whether or not
// setFog is set. Field-measured across a 0 -> 1 fog change, hazePars read
// bit-identical (0, 8e-5, 3.6e-4) - fog moved every one of its own lanes.
//
// The integral is the SAME SHAPE as the engine's fog term already
// implemented in the two fog blocks below, with two differences that are
// the whole reason a separate function exists:
//   1. the height gradient is SIGNED here (the fog term takes |dy|),
//   2. the base density is anchored at the CAMERA altitude, not at the
//      min of camera/pixel.
// Both read straight off the engine's own disassembly of the camera-above
// branch, which is the only branch a normal camera takes: the fog layer
// measured at -2 m (row 12 z + row 13 y = 0 + -2), so every above-water
// camera is above it. The camera-BELOW branch anchors at the layer instead
// and is left unimplemented deliberately - it is the underwater / raised-
// base case, it has never been observed in the field, and a guessed branch
// is exactly the "model shipped without a measurement" that has cost this
// project three builds. khaz_layerY is passed so it can be added later
// against a dump that actually flips it.
//
// setRenderDebug 60 zeroes hazePars.w on the CPU (dbgCtl.x carries only the
// 0-17 visual modes and all four dbg_ctl lanes are spoken for), so the A/B
// revert costs no CB field and no shader branch of its own.
