// 26325 THE VISIBLE BOX'S FOV IS ONE FRAME BEHIND ITS OWN FOOTPRINT, AND
// ONE IDENTITY IN dump1 PROVES IT: seamFovLatR[k] == injFovY[k+1] /
// injFovY[k] to within 1e-5 on 511 of 511 rows, peaking at 1.1775 through
// the zoom. Decomposed: the live bridge fetch carries frame k+1's
// projection scale terms, the cycle latch carries frame k's, the SEAM has
// taken the live pair since 26311, and inject_composited_meshes never has -
// its projection arbitration says so in its own comment, 'This switches
// only two projection scalars', meaning m22/m32 and nothing else. The
// footprint is therefore rasterised at the zoom the engine's volume pass
// computes with while the visible box is rasterised at the previous
// frame's, so the two diverge RADIALLY by the entire per-frame FOV delta
// (17.75 pct at the peak here). Along its own silhouette the box then
// consumes stencil counts and cascade verdicts authored for other pixels:
// the soldier's stencil shadow and the terrain cascades paint THROUGH it,
// oversized, in a band that breathes with the zoom and settles the instant
// the zoom stops. That is 26311's mechanism paragraph word for word, on the
// half 26311 did not touch - and it is why the artifact outlived the entire
// shooting-scale campaign yet now requires a zoom to appear: with the FOV
// static, frames k and k+1 carry the same scale and the divergence is
// identically zero, so every non-zooming session was a clean control.
//
// WHY NO LANE CAUGHT IT FOR ELEVEN BUILDS. reprojPx is the registration
// gauge and it is structurally blind here: it projects the box CENTRE
// through both matrices, and a pure scale difference is zero at the centre
// and grows toward the edges. It reads 0.2-8.8 px on the very rows
// seamFovLatR reads 1.17. seamFovLatR itself was shipped at 26315 as a
// gauge and filed 'low priority' by the campaign-44 handoff; it was the
// answer the whole time.
