// || 26334 (RenderDoc frame3430 on 26333; ledger at KH_BUILD_TAG): BOTH SURVIVORS MEASURED IN ONE CAPTURE, AND NEITHER WAS AN ENCODE QUESTION. Our draws located by CONSTANT-BLOCK NAME (CBObj) after entry points proved useless - DXBC normalises every entry to 'main' - giving inject eid 15667 (cycle A, DSV 975, 1 sample, zero colour targets) and the visible box eid 44006 (cycle B, DSV 973, 8x MSAA). (1) THE CLIP IS OUR OWN SLOPE-SCALED DEPTH BIAS. The box's 36 post-VS vertices span window z 0.9311491..0.9359962 and the draw WROTE 0.9289941; interpolated depth inside a triangle is convex and cannot leave the vertex envelope, so the 0.00215501 excess is applied bias, splitting 1.9073e-06 constant (0.09 pct) against 0.0021531 slope-scaled (99.91 pct) = MaxDepthSlope 0.0086124/px, a near-edge-on face. In metres that is 0.9 m toward the camera at 29 m and 3.7 m at 117 m (error grows as d^2/n): the box eats terrain and the soldier's lower body at range, worst from a high Zeus camera, flickering because the slope is recomputed per primitive per frame - and it survived 166/167/168 because it is rasterizer state, not a receive term. Caught directly at px 1982,746 and 1975,752 (bottom of the bbox) where our box beat an occluder NEARER than its own nearest vertex. DepthBiasClamp was 0 = NO CLAMP; the 26xxx reduction from -1.0 to -0.25 SCALED the pathology instead of BOUNDING it. KH_BIAS_CLAMP -4.0e-6 caps the worst case from 2.31 m to ~4 mm at 73 m and leaves the constant anti-shimmer duty intact. 179 = the unclamped twins. (2) THE SLICE IS THE WITNESS READING THE FARTHEST SAMPLE. KhWitLoad's real source is the PS t0 snapshot (tex 39962, R32_FLOAT, read off the BINDING - a format guess had picked engine tex 974 holding 78..148 and cost a round). On the 363 FULLY covered probe pixels the witness equals our surface EXACTLY (0.000000), so code 6 works in the interior; on the 139 MIXED-coverage silhouette pixels it equals the FARTHEST sample on 138 - the background - so membership fails, the 7x7 weight collapses, and KhVolSoftScene falls through to the RAW unwitnessed count. That fallthrough band along our silhouette IS the slice, and it is the raster-read failure the 26316 ledger describes, reinstated by a units-blind reduction. FIX: PSDepthResolve now emits TWO planes - .x farthest (the guard, byte-identical) and .y nearest (the witness, the correct reduction for 'is our surface present at this tap'). Taking .y is a measured NO-OP on every fully covered pixel and only acts in the silhouette band. 178 recompiles with WIT_NEAREST 0 = farthest into both planes = exactly 26333. ALSO ELIMINATED BY THE SAME CAPTURE: the MinDepth clamp (ndcZOutOfRange 0, wNeg 0, nothing written on the 0.011 floor - DepthClipEnable FALSE is armed but never engages), the presence family (502/502 probe pixels had occluder depth present before our box drew, 0 cleared), and the box-vs-injection MinDepth mismatch (both 0.011). AND A TOOL CORRECTION: the handoff-45 clip-signature recipe is FALSIFIED at Zeus ranges - on dump1 it fires on 239/512 rows, but gap/exp is near-constant at 0.197 and the fire rate is 0 pct below 20 m and ~100 pct above 50 m. It is a distance detector, not a clip detector; it discriminated on dump14/dump502 only because the box sat at 3-13 m there. Do not use it on Zeus dumps. ACCEPTANCE 26334: the box no longer renders through terrain or the soldier's lower body at any Zeus distance (179 restores it for the A/B); the silhouette slice is gone with the stencil ARMED on mode 0 (178 restores it); effectSetupFails 0; non-grazing and close-range behaviour visually unchanged.
// || 26335 (dump1 on 26334; ledger at KH_BUILD_TAG): 26334 BLINDED THE PROBES AND FIXED NEITHER ARTIFACT. THE REGRESSION FIRST: comp_depth_tex became R32G32_FLOAT at 26334, but the probe's readback staging is a hardcoded 3x1 R32_FLOAT and the map reads three CONSECUTIVE floats. D3D11 silently drops a CopySubresourceRegion between different format families, so every depth-probe lane died - prbCtrDM/GndDM/BotDM -1 and prbCtrDzM -99999 on 512/512 rows, where 26333's dump had 512/512 valid. The staging is now R32G32_FLOAT and the three samples are read at 0/2/4, taking .x so the lanes keep their historic meaning (resolved = farthest scene depth). LESSON, and it is the same one 26332 wrote down: a format change has CPU-side consumers, and a copy that D3D11 refuses does not raise - it just stops producing samples, exactly the failure mode the 26325 prbPre gauges were added to name. Audit every staging texture against its source format after ANY format change. FIELD ON 26334: both artifacts persist unchanged - the mirrored stencil along a thin edge and the flickery distance-dependent depth clip, and the operator adds a constraint no previous report carried: BOTH are confined to the LOWER PORTION of the box. That is new information and it does not fit either 26334 fix, both of whose mechanisms are uniform over the silhouette (the witness reduction) or over grazing faces (the slope bias) with no bottom-vs-top asymmetry. The 26334 changes are therefore NOT convicted by this round - they closed two measured defects that were real (the box wrote 0.9289941 against a 0.9311491 envelope; the witness matched the farthest sample on 138/139 mixed pixels) but neither was the author. Both stay in with their reverts (178/179) because both are correct on their own terms and neither can be shown harmful; do not spend a round re-litigating them. WHAT THE NEXT ROUND MUST DO: the artifact has never been LOCALISED. Every measurement so far has sampled a grid over the box's post-VS bbox or three fixed probe pixels, none of which is known to sit on an artifact pixel; the two 26334 convictions came from pixels that merely satisfied a signature. The decider is RenderDoc PixelHistory on operator-identified artifact pixels, which names every event that touched that pixel with its pre/post depth and shader output - it cannot be argued with and it does not need a model. Ask the operator for the artifact's pixel coordinates from the capture, then run it. NOTE ALSO: prbCnt reads a constant 255 and prbVolZ a per-session constant 0.99611 again this dump, and the box-owns-BOT check is meaningless while the probes are dead - re-baseline all of it on 26335 before reading anything into it.
// || 26336 (PixelHistory on capture frame3667; ledger at KH_BUILD_TAG): BOTH ARTIFACTS ARE THE ANALYTIC TERRAIN CLAMP'S IDENTITY GATE, AND THE WHOLE DEPTH-STAGE CAMPAIGN WAS THE WRONG STAGE. PSComposite writes SV_Depth, which REPLACES the rasterized depth entirely - so depth bias, DepthBiasClamp, DepthClipEnable and the viewport MinDepth floor cannot reach the visible box at all. 26334's clamp was operating on a value this draw discards, which is why it did not bind and why the 'bias excess' tracked camera angle instead of the clamp. That whole line of reasoning (26334 section 1) is WITHDRAWN; the excess I measured was never bias, it was the SV_Depth pull. WHAT IT ACTUALLY IS: the contact-band clamp spends khaOff = min(cap, (khaD - sceneZ) + 0.25) to drive our fragment in front of the competing depth, gated on an identity test that calls the competitor TERRAIN when its reconstructed world point sits within khaTol of the analytic heightfield. khaTol was max(1.0, cell*0.08) = EXACTLY 1.0 m on a 12.5 m grid. A soldier's boots, ankles, shins and knees are all inside 1 m of the ground, so the gate called a man's leg terrain and spent the pull against it. PixelHistory at 1922,1030 in writing: competitor 0.9685660, our own nearest vertex 0.9689184 (we should LOSE), we wrote 0.9681877. The torso and head clear the tolerance and are correctly refused - which is precisely why the operator only ever sees it on the LOWER PORTION, a confinement no other candidate in this campaign could explain. IT IS ALSO THE SLICE. Where the pull engages, khaODepth != i.pos.z by construction. The witness snapshot holds the WRITTEN SV_Depth while KhVolSoftScene compares against khStenP.x = i.pos.z, so membership fails, the 7x7 weight collapses and the filter falls through to the RAW unwitnessed count - the mirrored stencil, in the same band, at the same distances, flickering with the same terrain LOD. That is why the witness matched our surface EXACTLY (0.000000) on every fully-covered interior