// || 26337 (field on 26336; ledger at KH_BUILD_TAG): 26336 CONFIRMED THE MECHANISM AND LEFT TWO RESIDUALS, BOTH IN THE SAME BLOCK. Field verdict on 26336: the soldier show-through is largely gone at normal ranges - which convicts the identity tolerance exactly as 26336 argued and closes that question - but it returns AT EXTREME DISTANCE, on the WHOLE BODY rather than the parts inside khaTol, and intermittently. THE FAIL-OPEN IS WHY. KhThmHeight returns -1.0e6 for any point outside the uploaded heightfield window, and the gate left khaTerr at its initial TRUE in that case, so past the grid's edge the identity test stopped existing altogether and the pull was spent against whatever stood there at any height - hence whole body, hence only sometimes (it depends whether the reconstructed point lands inside the window), hence only far away. The 26186 fail-open was written for a missing input on the RESCUE path and does not survive being read as a licence to overtake an unidentified occluder. No sample now means NO PULL; 181 restores the fail-open. AND THE SLICE IS A UNITS MISMATCH WE HAVE BEEN LOOKING PAST FOR FOUR BUILDS. This chunk declares SV_Depth, so the value that reaches the depth buffer - and therefore the value the resolved witness snapshot holds - is khaODepth, which the contact clamp may have moved. khStenP was built from i.pos.z. Wherever the pull fires, those two differ by exactly the pull, so KhVolSoftScene's membership fails on precisely the fragments the pull touched, the 7x7 weight collapses, and it falls through to the RAW unwitnessed count - the mirrored stencil band. This is why 26336 fixed the depth artifact and not this one: the pull still fires LEGITIMATELY against real terrain at the contact band, which is exactly where the slice lives, and why the witness matched our surface to 0.000000 on every fully-covered interior pixel in three captures - outside the band the two values are byte-identical. khStenP.x now takes khaODepth; the gradient stays on