// encode - engine-exact for z >= near, a monotone ramp mapping [0, near)
// into [floor x KH_NEARZ_GAP_FRAC, floor) below it - and draw under a
// viewport whose MinDepth is widened to that gap floor so the ramp
// survives the clamp. Sub-near content orders among itself again, still
// beats all world content (it IS nearer than the near plane), and stays
// behind every weapon-partition write. Continuous at the near plane, so
// routing on/off never pops a fragment.
static constexpr float KH_NEARZ_GAP_FRAC = 0.92f;
// 26383 THE PASSTHROUGH IS GONE FROM MODE 0, AND THE SEAM WENT WITH
// IT. Field-confirmed on screen: at close range a thin line ran
// across our meshes, tracked the camera like a clip plane and removed
// nothing. Mode 185 located it - disarming the near-gap reroute makes
// the INSIDE of the mesh visible above that same line, which is
// 26001's near collapse and is the artifact the routing exists to
// remove - so the line is the near-gap BOUNDARY, the plane
// w == khr_nz_near (= -m32/m22 of the pass projection), camera-
// anchored, which is why it is close-range-only and why it follows
// the camera.
// WHY THE PASSTHROUGH WAS THE CAUSE: inside the boundary khaODepth
// comes from the near-gap ramp; outside it took i.pos.z verbatim.
// The two agree in VALUE at the boundary by construction (khr_nz_near
// is -m32/m22 of the same projection that fills depthParams.xy, so
// the outside ndc is identically 0 there and both sides land on
// depthParams.z) - but they are different EXPRESSIONS, and the
// recomputed side carries the [dp.z, dp.w] round-trip's rounding.
// At MinDepth ~0.011 on a D24 grid an ulp of disagreement is exactly
// hairline-sized. Recomputing BOTH sides makes them share the
// rounding and the line has nowhere to come from.
// WHY IT SHIPPED AS THE GATE ALONE AND NOT AS 51: mode 51 removed the
// seam too, but 51 is TWO changes - this gate AND the absolute NDC
// with its 1e-4 depth nudge. The nudge is a BIAS, and 26363/26364
// spent a campaign removing the last bias this file carried; the
// absolute form also costs 26184's precision on the terrain pull and
// the far-keep offsets. 26382 split them into one arm each and the
// field read the gate alone as sufficient. 51 keeps its own meaning
// (the formula) and is now orthogonal to this.
// COST OF THE FOLD: every arb-depth fragment takes the recomputed
// path instead of the raster passthrough. By 26184's own argument the
// delta form with a zero offset reproduces i.pos.z, so this is
// precision-neutral and adds no bias - the passthrough was an
// optimisation and a bit-exactness claim, not a correction.
// NON-REGRESSION at the fold (dump under the arm, 2173 flushes,
// nearzGapDraws 1751 with nearzRampFills 1751 - no routing without a
// fill): compositeSkips / RejVerify / RejFloor / AnomalySkips /
// arbNearDenied / encVpRejects / effectSetupFails / compFailStreak /
