// ENCODE FAR CEILING (log_new13 conviction - the box-beyond-view-distance
// residue): the engine runs a CELESTIAL/deep partition whose projection
// shares the world pair's NEAR (10-class at altitude) while its FAR runs
// two orders deeper (injDpM22 1.00006 / m32 -10.0006 decoded to far
// ~167 km against the world pair's ~2 km) - no near-based band, keep
// sanitization or pv-agreement rule can tell the two apart, and at
// certain heights the trigger-time slot carries the deep pair, so the
// INJECTION itself encoded through it: the PS far-contract boundary
// moved to 167 km and the non-farVis box drew far beyond the view
// distance. The discriminator is absolute: the engine's overall view
// distance caps at 40 km, the celestial partition runs far beyond it.
// Any pair whose derived far exceeds this ceiling is refused at every
// ENCODE acceptance point (injection slot rung + far-phase arming, the
// keep's write sanitization, the flush slot rung, and as referee
// hygiene in the flush far-drift test and the injection's latch-vs-live
// resolve). The raw slot keeps flowing to the far-phase distance test
// and anomaly classification exactly as ledgered - only encode
// AUTHORSHIP is gated.
static constexpr float KH_ENC_FAR_MAX = 50000.0f;

// ===========================================================================
// 26199 ENCODE NEAR-CLASS AGREEMENT (the underwater punch-through).
//
// MEASURED, two dumps, one variable. Same pose, camera dropped from -26.1 m
// to -74.7 m; at -26.1 the boxes are correctly occluded by the water, at
// -74.7 they draw through it. The shipped injection pair moved:
//     occluded:  m22 1.00001  m32 -0.0957148  -> near  0.0957 m
//     through:   m22 1.00050  m32 -10.005     -> near 10.0050 m
// A HUNDREDFOLD near change. Everything else exculpates itself in the same
// pair of dumps: modes 10/11/12 read cyan and BLACK in both, so khaOff is
// exactly zero and the analytic clamp, the contact band and khaTol are all
// innocent; snapFails 0, injGuardOff 4 vs 5, flushFallbackDraws 2 in both.
//
// Why it got through: every encode rung gates on an absolute near BAND
// [KH_CAM_NEAR_MIN, KH_CAM_NEAR_MAX] = [0.05, 15] plus a far CEILING. A
// 10.005 near sits inside the band and its ~20 km far is under the ceiling,
// so nothing refused it. The KH_ENC_FAR_MAX ledger describes the mirror of
// this fault - a partition sharing the world NEAR with a far two orders
// deeper - and closed it with an absolute far ceiling. This is the same
// fault reflected: a partition sharing the far class with a near two orders
// shallower, and an absolute band cannot see it either.
//
// The discriminator is NOT a constant. The projection census already ranks
// pairs by sightings, and the world pair dominates it in both dumps (1964
// and 213 hits at near 0.0957) while the near-10 class carries ONE hit. So
// the reference is measured per session: encode authorship is refused when
// the candidate's near differs from the most-sighted pair's near by more
// than an ORDER OF MAGNITUDE. That is a class test, not a tuning knob - a
// stale bridge or a legitimate near change moves the near by percents, and
// the census's own top pair follows it within a cycle.
//
// FAILURE MODE, deliberately bounded: a refusal falls back to the MEASURED
// sniffer pair, or failing that the bridge pv - the pre-slot-optimisation
// path. Worst case is a one-frame-stale projection, which is delay class,
// against a mesh punching through water, which is artifact class. It can
// only ever REFUSE an override; it never authors a value of its own.
// setRenderDebug 65 reverts. Ledger: encNearClassRejects / encNearRefM.
// ===========================================================================
static constexpr float KH_ENC_NEAR_CLASS = 10.0f;   // order-of-magnitude bar
static uint64_t g_enc_near_class_rejects = 0;
