// KH_BLK_SHADE_LATCH - 26417 THE BLACK BOX, MEASURED WHERE IT ACTUALLY LANDS.
//
// 26416 established that the black box is NOT a dark publish: the operator saw
// one while every detector built for it read its null value (blkDarkFirstS /
// LastS / ReseedSl / SpanS / StdSl and ffrDarkAgeS all -1; blkDarkPubRefusals,
// Reseeds, SeedBlocks, ForceAdopts, CollapseHolds, StarvedAdopts, IncohHolds
// all 0; meshDarkFrames 0; the per-row dark and erased lanes 0 on 512 of 512).
// Seven campaigns of gates have watched the PUBLISH path and the event is not
// on it. And the one number section 3.4 waited for turned out to falsify its
// own plan: blkAcceptRatioMin 0.334956 is a 2.985x collapse on an ORDINARY
// publish against a 2.79x black-box event, so no ratio bar can separate them.
//
// SO THIS MEASURES SOMETHING ELSE ENTIRELY: what the SHADER WAS HANDED. Not
// what was published, not what was refused, not what the probe thinks the
// scene is - the actual bytes in the frame CB that the box shades from. If
// the box is black then this number is small, whatever the publish path
// believed, and if it is NOT small then the darkness is downstream of the
// lighting block and every lane in the blk family is looking at the wrong
// subsystem - which is itself the answer.
//   shade = max(sun.rgb) + max(amb.rgb), taken at the fill, every frame.
// It is deliberately NOT gated, thresholded or arbitrated. A gauge with a
// gate in it is how blkDarkPubRefusals came to read 0 through a live event.
//
// THE LATCH IS THE POINT, and it is the 26414 band-table pattern that closed
// the cascade in one dump. The event is rare and short; a session total or a
// last-frame snapshot will never contain it. Everything below is captured AT
// THE DARKEST FRAME OF THE SESSION and kept: the block's own rgb, the source
// flags, the lit gate, the shadow strength, the sun-map state, and - the pair
// that decides it - the STANDING probe luminances at that same instant.
//
// PRE-REGISTERED READING, written before the dump (rule 1.1):
//   blkShadeMin near 0 with blkShadeStdSun/StdAmb HEALTHY -> the block handed
//     to the shader is dark while the scene is lit. The fault is between the
//     probe and this fill: g_pub_block_* is the snapshot, so it is the
//     snapshot or its publish gate, and blkShadeValid says whether the fill
//     even took the published branch or fell to the flat-white cold path.
//   blkShadeMin near 0 with the standing pair ALSO near 0 -> the probe itself
//     believes the world is dark. The fault is upstream in the locator, and
//     blkShadeProbeAgeS says whether it had simply gone stale.
//   blkShadeMin HEALTHY through a black-box event -> the lighting block is
//     exonerated outright and the darkness is downstream: the shadow terms
//     (blkShadeStrength, blkShadeSunOk), the lit gate (blkShadeLitGate), or
//     the material path. That would retire the entire blk family as the wrong
//     axis, which after seven campaigns is worth more than another gate.
// blkShadeDarkFrames counts frames under a tenth of the session's own
// brightest - self-anchored, so it needs no constant and cannot be tuned into
// agreeing with anybody.
// ==========================================================================
// ==========================================================================
// 26418 THE BLACK BOX IS AN UNPOPULATED SUN, AND THE LATCH CAUGHT IT WHOLE.
//
// THE EVENT, latched at the darkest frame (blkShadeT 32.737 s):
//   blkShadeSunR/G/B  0 / 0 / 0          EXACTLY zero, all three channels
//   blkShadeAmbR/G/B  0 / 0.0110 / 0.0354
//   blkShadeMin 0.0353 against blkShadeMax 9.0132   - a 255x collapse
//   blkShadeValid 1     the fill took the PUBLISHED branch, not the cold path
//   blkShadeStdSun 0    the standing probe agrees the sun is zero
//   blkShadeProbeAgeS 2.29e-05  the locator had JUST confirmed - not stale
//   blkShadeDarkFrames 968 of 2668
// THE LATCH IS WHY THIS EXISTS AT ALL: the trace ring spans ageS 0.01 to
// 12.72 s and every row in it is healthy (blkSunLum 17.07-19.92 on 512 of
// 512). The event at 32.7 s is twenty seconds older than the oldest row in
// the window. No per-row lane could ever have seen it, which is exactly what
// 26416 concluded from the whole blkDark family reading its null value.
//
// WHAT IT IS. A sun of EXACTLY (0, 0, 0) on all three channels is not a
// lighting state - there is no time of day, weather or altitude in this
// engine that produces an identically zero sun colour beside a nonzero
// ambient. It is an UNPOPULATED block: the locator anchored on the altitude
// lane, the anchor matched, the block was adopted and published, and its sun
// lanes had not been written yet. The healthy population never comes near it
// (blkShadeMax 9.0132; per-row blkSunLum 17.07 minimum across the whole ring),
// so this is not a threshold sitting inside a population - it is a distinct
// value that only the fault produces. Rule 1.2 has nothing to bite on: the
// test is an exact zero, not a bar.
//
// WHY IT SELF-HEALS AFTER ~30 s, which the operator's "recovers eventually"
// has always described: 968 dark frames of 2668 at roughly 40 flushes per
// second is about 24 s, at the START of a ~66 s session. The engine populates
// the block eventually and everything downstream corrects itself.
//
// THE FIX IS ABSENT-BEATS-WRONG, the standing doctrine, and it costs nothing:
// a block whose sun is exactly zero is REFUSED, and the fill takes the branch
// it already has for the never-published case - flat white sun over scalar
// ambient, with light_amb.w 0 so every downstream consumer knows. A box lit
// flat for the first half-minute is a far smaller error than a black one, and
// it is the same trade 26380's own ledger makes for the sub-second cold
// window. 99 REVERTS.
// blkZeroSunRefusals IS THE ENGAGEMENT LANE (rule 1.16): if it reads 0 the
// gate never fired and any null result is void - the one lesson 26378, 26403
// and 26413 each paid for separately.
// WHAT IT DOES NOT CLAIM: that every black box is this. It claims that THIS
// event was an exactly-zero sun reaching the shader, which is measured, and
// that refusing it cannot make anything worse, which is construction. If a
// black box recurs with blkZeroSunRefusals climbing, the zero is being
// refused and the darkness has a second source.
// 26612 PREMISE CORRECTION (KH_NIGHT_ZERO_SUN; ledger at the fill's gate):
// 'no lighting state produces an identically zero sun colour' is FALSE at
// deep night - dump1-26611 reads the engine's standing sun at exactly 0
// with ambient 0.0186 - and 'refusing it cannot make anything worse' fails
// with it: the refusal shipped flat white all night (the glowing mesh).
// The refusal now applies only against a standing sun > 0.5 or an unknown
// standing (the cold window this gate was built for); a measured-dark
// standing admits the block. Mode 385 restores 26418 verbatim.
// ==========================================================================
