// 26144 LAST-FIRE CLAMP (campaign-25 closure; dump5 conviction, DEFAULT).
// dbg 40 settled the mechanism: one effective paint per frame killed the
// duplicate outright (fireSingleSuppressed 12472, ghost gone in both views).
// So the second copy was always one of the frame's own extra same-index
// fires, and no camera on any of the three freeze sources was ever going to
// remove it. But dbg 40 kept the FIRST fire, and that lost the shadow
// entirely on a static look-down while standing on it, below a pitch
// threshold - which is the same asymmetry the 26134 ledger already recorded
// from the other side ("the mode-32 look-down dimness independently proves
// the final near/look-down paint is the LAST re-fire's"). Read together:
// the frame's fires are NOT redundant - the near/look-down content is
// covered by the LAST fire and the ordinary view by the first, which is
// exactly why keeping either one alone leaves a hole and keeping both
// paints the ghost.
// The clamp therefore keeps exactly one paint and makes it the LAST one.
// The last fire cannot be identified while it is happening, so the index is
// LEARNED from the previous frame and self-corrects: a frame that ends with
// no paint at all lowers the target immediately (never below 1), and any
// frame that paints re-learns the target from its own final count. Stable
// fire counts converge to exactly one paint - the last - within a frame.
// setRenderDebug 22 disables the clamp (every fire paints - the pre-26144
// ghosting behaviour); setRenderDebug 40 keeps the FIRST fire instead (the
// dump5 A/B).
