// 26156 LOCK IDENTITY ACROSS THE DEATH (task 2A - the last open question).
// dump118 (during the fault) and dump8 (same session, 60 s later) settle
// everything except one thing, and they settle it hard:
//   viewRelockTmagMin 0        - the remembered source is EXACTLY
//     camera-relative. It is the real view CB and it never went away.
//   viewRelockProbes 455288    - it is uploaded and scored continuously
//     through the whole dead window.
//   viewRelockErMin 0.0427861  - and its best agreement with the bridge
//     never once falls below that, in either dump, to six figures. With
//     injRotDeltaMaxDeg 0.056 the camera was effectively still, so this is
//     a STANDING offset, not the one-frame bridge lag.
// The relock probe demands 1e-3. That is 43x unreachable, so the probe is
// dead code in this failure mode - viewRelocks 0 in both dumps, and it was
// 0 in dump59 and dump50 before them. Recovery came instead from a FRESH
// ring lock: viewLocks 1 -> 2, lockWipes 1 -> 2, and it took ~42 s (drop at
// 4.78 s, coldFirstCast 47.47 s). THAT is the cold-start slowness, in one
// number, and 2A is what the screen shows during it.
// One question decides the fix, and it is not answerable from any counter
// that exists: did the ring come back to the SAME (res, off) it was
// dropped from?
//   SAME slot  -> the guard force-dropped a lock that was correct all
//     along, spent 42 s re-deriving it, and the repair belongs at the
//     guard - hysteresis, or a recovery bar that is not stricter than the
//     bar that did the dropping.
//   OTHER slot -> the guard was right, lock 1 really was the subtly-wrong
//     CB slot it exists to catch, and the entire defect is re-acquisition
//     latency in the ring hunt. Repair moves there and the guard is left
//     alone.
// Both repairs are cheap. Building the wrong one costs a build and a field
// session, which is the exact pattern the method note indicts. So this
// build asks, and ships no repair.
static const void* g_view_lock_res_pre = nullptr;   // lock identity as of the last DROP
static uint32_t g_view_lock_off_pre = 0;
static int      g_view_lock_orient_pre = 0;   // matches LiveShadowState::view_src_orient (int)
static uint32_t g_view_lock_same_slot = 0;   // 0 no lock since a drop, 1 SAME slot, 2 different
static uint32_t g_view_lock_acq_path = 0;    // path of the last acquisition:
                                             // 1 relock probe, 2 injection prewarm, 3 ring hunt
static uint64_t g_view_lock_acq_ms = 0;      // stamp of the last acquisition
static float    g_view_lock_dead_s = -1.0f;  // drop -> re-acquire latency (the 42 s)
static float    g_view_lock_dead_max_s = 0.0f;
