// 26369 THE CASCADE'S OWN REGISTRATION, WHICH NOTHING HAS EVER REPORTED.
// The operator reports cascades briefly ANCHORING TO THE CAMERA - offset,
// then settling about a second later - and flickering out entirely on fast
// abrupt movement. 26367 gave the age lanes and they answered half of it:
// bandPickAgeMs reaches 913.9 ms, which is the "settles a second later" to
// the millisecond. But dump4 also killed the obvious cause - the steady-frame
// maximum (884.7) EXCEEDS the transient maximum (762.0), so the staleness is
// NOT caused by motion, and an age alone cannot say whether a stale band is
// MISREGISTERED or merely old. A band baked a second ago from a camera that
// has not moved is perfectly correct.
// "Anchored to the camera" is a REGISTRATION error, and BandSlot already
// carries what measures it: vcol, the view matrix the slot was baked with.
// Recovering that camera and differencing it against the pass's own gives
// the cascade the lane primeCamDxM gives the seam - which is the lane that
// finally convicted the stencil offset at 26366.
// PURE GAUGE. Nothing reads it; mode 0 is byte-identical to 26368.
// GUARDED, not assumed: vcol is documented as the view's columns 0..2 in
// row-vector convention, so each column's first three components are an
// orthonormal basis row and the fourth is the translation. If any column's
// norm leaves [0.9, 1.1] the layout is not what the comment says and the
// lane publishes -1 rather than a number computed through a wrong transpose
// - which is exactly how 26342 lost a round.
// PRE-REGISTERED:
//   bandPickCamDxM ~ 0 while bandPickAgeMs is large
//     => the band is old but correctly registered, the age lanes are a red
//        herring, and the flicker is a CONTENT problem (pool/pick), not a
//        transform one. bandPoolMissN and bandPickNoneN are then the axis.
//   bandPickCamDxM tracking the camera's travel over bandPickAgeMs
//     => the band is being displayed against a camera it was not baked for,
//        which IS "anchored to the camera", and the fold is to refuse a slot
//        whose baked camera has moved beyond a bound - the same shape as the
//        seam's trajectory bound, which already works.
//   bandPickCamDxM large while bandPickAgeMs is small
//     => the slot is being sealed against the wrong view in the first place,
//        which is a staging fault and not a staleness one at all.
// ==========================================================================
// 26375: the alternative. A registration bound at the band pick is only a
// fix if refusing has somewhere to GO - the loop breaks straight after the
// assignment, so refusing simply continues to the next (coarser) band, and
// if none qualifies g_band_pick stays 0, which IS bandPickNone: the cascade
// vanishes. That would trade the offset symptom for the flicker-out
// symptom. These two lanes say whether the fallback is real BEFORE any
// bound is chosen, and they need no threshold to do it.
static float    g_band_alt_cam_dx_m = -1.0f;  // best OTHER valid slot's registration
static uint32_t g_band_alt_better = 0;        // how many are better than the pick
static float    g_band_pick_cam_dx_m = -1.0f;
static float    g_band_pick_cam_dx_max = 0.0f;
static uint64_t g_band_pick_cam_bad = 0;    // vcol failed the orthonormal check
static float    g_band_pick_age_ms = -1.0f; // seal age of the winner, last cycle
static float    g_band_pick_age_max_ms = 0.0f;
static float    g_band_pick_vz = 0.0f;      // its view-z, last cycle
