// over the 1 px bar - so the gate REFUSES every frame that needs the carry.
// And it opens on the static tails (camStepM ~0.003, 1.8 px) where
// firePaintPath is CONSTANT for hundreds of frames and nothing is wrong.
// THE REASON IS PHYSICAL, not a tuning miss: the arm mode is set by what the
// engine draws, so it only switches when the camera moves. Static blocks
// never transition, never flicker, and never need a carry. The flicker and
// the double do not merely share a motion term - they are the SAME motion.
// There is no threshold that separates them and the quadrant is EMPTY.
// This is the 26160 trap again (extrapolation placed inside a test that never
// tripped), caught this time by reading the enclosing condition against the
// data BEFORE a field round instead of after one.
// The carry family is now closed on arithmetic rather than on taste. DEFAULT
// IS OFF - the build is 26165 single paint, verbatim. setRenderDebug 42
// enables it for anyone who wants to see the effect; fireCarryPaints will be
// nonzero only while standing still, which is exactly when it is useless.
// Kept as code because a documented dead end with the numbers attached is
// worth more than a sentence saying somebody once considered it.
