// ==========================================================================
// 26265 THE LOCATOR SWEEPS THE DRAW STREAM INSTEAD OF SITTING ON ONE DRAW.
//
// Five locator defects across 26257-26262 were all reasoning about WHICH draw
// carries the view. 26260 moved the stage from the resolve to the seam and
// 26263 measured that the seam's bound state is not the capture's either. The
// handoff's step 1 was to settle that with a capture - but the question only
// exists because the locator gets ONE draw per frame and it is always the same
// draw. Sample the stream instead and the question disappears: the address is
// a property of the shader family, so ANY family that binds the view buffer
// will do, and the copy finds the resource by identity afterwards regardless
// of which slot that family used.
//
// This is the cascbind_step / skybind_step pattern that already works in this
// file (lightLocOff located, lightLocMisses 0). Divided sampling, capped per
// frame, and it SELF-DISARMS: once located it drops to a slow re-confirm rate
// whose only job is to notice the address moving (engFpDrifts).
