                        // ======================================================
                        // 26405 THE 2 CM LINE IS SITTING ON TOP OF A WALKING
                        // START, AND dump3 PUTS TWELVE OF THEM UNDER IT.
                        //
                        // 26402 fixed the RATIO branch and the artifact survived,
                        // which looked like the axis being wrong again. It was not:
                        // it was the OTHER branch, and dump3 is the session that
                        // separates them because the operator replicated the jump
                        // repeatedly ON FOOT rather than in a vehicle.
                        // ALL TWELVE REFUSALS ARE ONE EVENT, TO FOUR DECIMALS:
                        //   camStepM[k-1] = 0.0000 exactly   (a dead stop)
                        //   camStepM[k]   = 0.0174 .. 0.0190 (the first walk frame)
                        //   camStepM[k+1] = 0.5366 .. 0.5830 (walking speed)
                        //   bnd           = 0.3000 on all 12 (the FLOOR branch)
                        //   primeCamDxM[k+1] == camStepM[k+1] on all 12
                        // The sim's first frame of walk motion is 1.7-1.9 cm. The
                        // 2 cm "still" line was argued as "below 2 cm nothing
                        // legitimate can produce a 0.30 m jump" - and the whole
                        // legitimate population sits 1-3 mm underneath it, in a
                        // 1.6 mm band. That is 26252's title applied to a second
                        // threshold: at the EDGE of a population, not in the GAP.
                        //
                        // THE OPERATOR'S DESCRIPTION IS THE MECHANISM, and it is
                        // what finally named this. The stencil cast by a soldier
                        // onto the box jumps TOWARDS the unit when the camera moves
                        // BACK and OUTWARDS when it moves FORWARD, and on the
                        // outward frame the shape reads as the shadow that would
                        // land on the GROUND UNDER the box. A refusal holds the
                        // LATCH, so the footprint is drawn one camera step behind
                        // the colour pass. Moving forward, the stale footprint sits
                        // at a LARGER view depth than the box actually has, so the
                        // engine's z-fail counting resolves our pixels against a
                        // receiver BEHIND the box - which is the ground - and we
                        // read the ground's shadow at the box's pixels. Moving
                        // back, the sign flips and the receiver is too NEAR, which
                        // walks the shape toward the caster. One mechanism, both
                        // directions, and the sign flip is the thing no lateral
                        // camera fault can produce. It is a DEPTH error, which is
                        // why every positional gauge on this axis stayed clean.
                        //
                        // THE VALUE IS PLACED IN A MEASURED GAP, NOT PICKED. The
                        // foreign class the floor exists for is ser 3642: 2.593 m
                        // off a reference of 0.001. The legitimate class is
                        // 0.0174-0.0190. Those are 17-19x apart with nothing
                        // between them, and 0.005 sits ~3.5x above one and ~3.5x
                        // below the other. The floor's job is untouched: a 0.001
                        // reference still takes the 0.30 m floor and still refuses
                        // 2.593 m with 8.6x to spare. A reference just above the
                        // new line gets 100 x 0.005 = 0.50 m, which a 2.593 m
                        // foreign jump still fails by 5x.
                        // 221 RESTORES 0.02. ACCEPTANCE: seamTrnEvent 1 goes to 0
                        // on walking starts, primeCamDxM 0 on every row, and the
                        // towards/outwards jump gone in BOTH directions - that last
                        // one is the only acceptance that has ever mattered here.
